{"_id":"APOFa001Yandee","name":"Yandee","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":55,"max":55},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":4},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":65,"instinct":80,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Vor of the Golyanovo II Bratva</strong></p><p>(Secretly) an android built from scraps on a prison world, Yandee rose through the ranks of the powerful Golyanovo II Bratva empire by discovering the lucrative Sycorax trade. Methodical.</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> Laser Pistol 1d100 DMG</p><h3>What Can You Do For Them?</h3><ul><li>The Babushka is late on protection money. Go collect. 500cr.</li><li>[Strike 1] Assassinate head of The Syndicate. 2mcr.</li><li>[Strike 2] Destroy the Conquer All. Make it look like an accident. 1mcr.</li><li>[Strike 2] Escort Teamster scabs to work. 50kcr/day.</li><li>[Unrest 2] Find the Sycorax formula in Farm Two. 20mcr and a ship.</li><li>[Outbreak 3] Kill Caliban. 50mcr.</li><li>Harvest Sycorax. 10kcr/3 fruit.</li><li>Do 3 jobs for Yandee and become a Novo Droog. 10kcr/month.</li></ul>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa002Angus","name":"Angus","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":20,"max":20},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":2},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":25,"instinct":75,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Sysadmin of CANYONHEAVY.market</strong></p><p>Runs the sector's most powerful data brokerage firm and the intelligence arm of the Golyanovo II Bratva. Loyal to Yandee. Always has a lead on work for a 1d10kcr finder's fee. Chatty, manic voice.</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> Revolver 1d10+1 DMG</p><h3>What Can You Do For Them?</h3><ul><li>Always looking for good information. Tips pay 3d10kcr/ea.</li><li>[Strike 1] Location of Stratemeyer Syndicate. 200kcr.</li><li>[Unrest 1] Find who is broadcasting the Hunglung Footage. 250kcr.</li><li>[Outbreak 1] Investigate rumors of girl named Ariel haunting the Slickbays. 20kcr.</li><li>[Strike 2] Negotiate with Reidmar. See if he'll end the strike before Yandee sheds blood. 500kcr.</li><li>Hack The Babushka's OGRE. 5mcr.</li></ul>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa003Reidmr","name":"Reidmar","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":20,"max":20},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":3},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":35,"instinct":55,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Union Rep of Teamster Local 32819L</strong></p><p>Union loyalist, fluid expression of their gruff exterior and notoriously impatient. Legendary pilot. Distributes Yandee's Sycorax to fund Local 32819L's corporate lobbying. Rough voice.</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> Spanner 2d10 DMG</p><h3>What Can You Do For Them?</h3><ul><li>[Strike 1] Locate the Stratemeyer Syndicate hideout where the lost fleet is being held hostage. 50kcr.</li><li>[Strike 1] Provide protection for the Teamsters during negotiations with Yandee. 100kcr.</li><li>[Strike 2] Sabotage scab freighters attempting to leave port. 75kcr per ship disabled/destroyed.</li><li>[Unrest 2] Smuggle weapons into The Choke. 500kcr/smuggling run.</li><li>[Outbreak 2] Help evacuate The Dream. Normal ship's charter +50kcr/Evacuation run.</li></ul>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa004Brunhl","name":"Brunhildh","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":45,"max":45},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":3},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":70,"instinct":65,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Chief Adjudicator of The Court</strong></p><p>Retired bounty hunter overseeing The Court. Yandee's fanatic right hand. Feared interrogator. Settled here for quality Big Switch and combat. Uses a modded antique blunderbuss (2mcr).</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> Blunderbuss 6d10 DMG</p><h3>What Can You Do For Them?</h3><ul><li>Find out if Cutter is loyal to Yandee. 1mcr for hard evidence.</li><li>Playtest new Slicksquid design. Survive and become an honorary Executioner.</li><li>[Unrest 2] Locate and apprehend Imogene Kane. Alive. 2mcr.</li><li>[Outbreak 2] The Court needs Chokespawn for the Pit. 100kcr/ea. Alive only.</li><li>[Strike 3] Protect Yandee from Teamsters and get them off The Dream. 50kcr. Become Novo Captain.</li><li>Act as Public Defender. 5kcr/win.</li></ul>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa005Cutter","name":"Commander Cutter","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":50,"max":50},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":3},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":75,"instinct":55,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Commander of Tempest Company</strong></p><p>Established his command as a privateer during the Corp Wars. Widely feared as a salt-the-earth tactician. Security arm of the Golyanovo II Bratva. Doesn't trust Yandee. Unrelenting voice.</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> Pulse Rifle 3d10 DMG</p><h3>What Can You Do For Them?</h3><ul><li>[Unrest 1] Find the Hunglungs who bombed the station. 250kcr.</li><li>[Unrest 2] Arrest Ukko/Ukka. Gain a Rank in Tempest Co. 40kcr.</li><li>[Outbreak 2] Hunt Chokespawn. Given an Exosuit and 500cr/kill.</li><li>[Strike 3] Kill Reidmar. Gain a Rank in Tempest Co. and your own 5 member Operator Squad.</li><li>[Unrest 3] Defeat the Hunglung Insurgency. Kill Imogene Kane. Promoted to Platoon Commander. 1mcr.</li><li>(Secret) Kill Novo Droogs. 10kcr/kill.</li></ul>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa006UkkoUk","name":"Ukko/Ukka","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":20,"max":20},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":2},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":20,"instinct":60,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>High Gardener of Invictus Sol</strong></p><p>Born in Doptown, Ukko/Ukka harvested Sycorax to pay off their birth debt. Joined the Solarians as a chemist, rose quickly to High Gardener. Donates massive O2 to The Choke. Coughs.</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> Unarmed</p><h3>What Can You Do For Them?</h3><ul><li>Always looking for Public Defenders for the oxy-poor. Can pay in drug supply.</li><li>[Strike 1] Negotiate a deal between The Novos and Local 32819L. 100kcr.</li><li>[Outbreak 1] Investigate rumors of a \"Dr. Bancali\" in The Choke. 40kcr.</li><li>[Unrest 2] Smuggle Ukko/Ukka off The Dream before Tempest Co. can kill them. The Solarian Church will owe you.</li><li>[Outbreak 3] Destroy the infected Aarnivalkea. Crew is given a Solarian shuttle.</li><li>Donate O2 to Doptown.</li></ul>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa007Loshe","name":"Loshe","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":40,"max":40},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":3},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":55,"instinct":60,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Dockmaster</strong></p><p>Loshe personally oversees every ship that comes in. This makes him a hub of information about who's who aboard The Dream.</p><p>Speaks in a calm voice. Always smokes cigars. Drinks Cadre Cola. In recovery.</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> Exoskeleton Bash 4d10 DMG</p><p><strong>Special - Exoskeleton:</strong> Four arms, each capable of attacking or firing a weapon in one round. Reapable. Worth 300kcr.</p><h3>What Does He Want?</h3><ul><li>To keep the dock running smoothly and without injury.</li><li>To get his 1 year sobriety chip.</li><li>To protect the Union. Despises corruption.</li></ul>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa008Indyl","name":"Indyl","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":15,"max":15},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":5},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":35,"instinct":85,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Procurer - Runs The Ecstasy</strong></p><p>Tall and graceful. Staunchly protective of their workers. Covered in esoteric motion-tattoos. Indyl's personal bodyguards, the Seraphs of Virtue, are highly skilled assassins with an 85% clearance rate who can be hired for 2mcr/target.</p><p><strong>Weapons:</strong> Retractable Nanoblade 2d10 DMG or Laser Pistol 1d100 DMG</p><p><strong>Pheromone Transmitter:</strong> Body Save or [-] to acting against Indyl.</p><p><strong>Poison Tongue:</strong> After a successful hit Indyl can use their tongue like a poisonous stinger. Body Save at [-] or be paralyzed for 1d10 hours.</p><p><strong>MODS:</strong> Retractable Nanoblade (10kcr), Poison Tongue (400kcr), Pheromone Transmitter (2.5mcr).</p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa009Babush","name":"The Babushka","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":45,"max":45},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":2},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":25,"instinct":90,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Cybersurgeon</strong></p><p>Legendary cybersurgeon. Intensely private. Clinically removed from her patients, but generally has a good heart. Doesn't speak much, letting Zhenya, her holographic AI child, do most of the talking.</p><p><strong>Weapons:</strong> Sawed-Off Combat Shotgun 2d10+2 DMG or MegaTranq Rifle 1d10 DMG (Body Save [-] or fall unconscious)</p><p><strong>Cyber Savant:</strong> When she hits with any weapon, she can shut down any one of the target's cybermod for the duration of the encounter.</p><p><strong>MODS:</strong> Unknown. Assume everything.</p><p><strong>POSSESSIONS:</strong> Bag of useless junk.</p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa010Bancal","name":"Dr. Bancali","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":20,"max":20},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":2},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":65,"instinct":65,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>The Doctor</strong></p><p>Bancali is singularly devoted to curing someone named Ariel of a rare and terminal disease which he only calls \"her sickness.\" He is the last remaining scrap of Caliban's sanity, compartmentalized in an advanced home-grown sleeve. He is unaware of the damage Caliban is causing, or the ACMD outbreak.</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> Scalpel 1d10 + Infection Save</p><p>A gross orifice in the wall of his lab opens onto a tunnel to The Atrium. Bancali cautions the players \"not to go poking around in his heart.\" Bancali will install cybernetic \"gills\" that remove the need to breathe oxygen if asked.</p><p><strong>Warning:</strong> If Bancali is killed, Caliban loses control (move to Outbreak: Phase 3).</p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa011QTeam","name":"Q-Team Member","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":20,"max":20},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":2},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":25,"instinct":25,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Quarantine Team</strong></p><p>Hazmat clad brutes who strip search and spray newcomers with disinfectant.</p><p><strong>Weapons:</strong> Disinfectant Foam Gun (Body Save or be knocked down) or Pulse Rifle 3d10 DMG</p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa012TmpPrb","name":"Tempest Co. Probie","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":35,"max":35},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":2},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":25,"instinct":25,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Tempest Company - Rank 1</strong></p><p>Entry-level Tempest mercenary assigned to a fireteam.</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> SMG 2d10 DMG</p><p><strong>Tactics:</strong> Takes cover, calls for reinforcements.</p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa013TmpOpr","name":"Tempest Co. Operator","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":35,"max":35},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":2},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":35,"instinct":25,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Tempest Company - Ranks 2-5</strong></p><p>Full fledged member of Tempest Co.</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> Pulse Rifle 3d10 DMG</p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa014TmpArm","name":"Tempest Co. Armored Trooper","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":20,"max":20},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":3},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":65,"instinct":45,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":13,"max":13},"description":"<p><strong>Tempest Company - Ranks 8-9</strong></p><p>Elite drop soldiers and deep recon scouts.</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> GPMG 4d10 DMG + Frag Grenades</p><p><strong>Damage Reduction:</strong> 5</p><p><strong>Armor Points:</strong> 13</p><p><strong>Exosuit:</strong> [+] on Strength Checks, x2 O2 tanks. Worth 40kcr.</p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa015NovDrg","name":"Novo Droog","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":20,"max":20},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":1},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":55,"instinct":25,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Golyanovo II Bratva Enforcer</strong></p><p>Street-level thugs working for Yandee's criminal empire.</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> Knives 1d10 DMG or Shotgun 4d10 DMG</p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa016Hunglg","name":"Hunglung Insurgent","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":20,"max":20},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":1},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":35,"instinct":25,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Doptown Resistance Fighter</strong></p><p>Revolutionary fighters from The Choke, led by Imogene Kane.</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> Old SMGs 2d10 DMG or Spears 1d10+1 DMG</p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa017Execut","name":"Executioner","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":35,"max":35},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":3},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":55,"instinct":35,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>The Court's Elite Fighters</strong></p><p>Combat specialists who serve The Court and Chief Adjudicator Brunhildh.</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> Electrolash 2d10 DMG</p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa018Seraph","name":"Seraph of Virtue","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":20,"max":20},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":3},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":70,"instinct":65,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Indyl's Personal Assassins</strong></p><p>Highly skilled assassins with an 85% clearance rate who can be hired for 2mcr/target.</p><p><strong>Weapons:</strong> Electrified Lash 2d10 DMG or Smart Rifle 4d10 DMG (AA)</p><p><strong>Tactics:</strong> Ambush, retreat, repeat.</p><p><strong>Electrified Lash:</strong> Body Save or fall unconscious.</p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa019Gundrn","name":"Gundrone","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":15,"max":15},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":1},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":60,"instinct":25,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Security Drone</strong></p><p>Flying automated security drones used at The Stellar Burn.</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> SMG 2d10 DMG</p><p><strong>Special:</strong> Flying</p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa020Chkspn","name":"Chokespawn (Basic)","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":20,"max":20},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":2},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":50,"instinct":45,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>ACMD Infected Creature</strong></p><p>Horrific fusion of organic and cybernetic tissue, created by the ACMD virus and controlled by Caliban.</p><p><strong>Weapon:</strong> Varies (2d10 DMG typical)</p><p>Roll on the Chokespawn table (pg. 35) for specific form, unique feature, and special attack.</p><h3>Creating a Chokespawn</h3><p>Roll 1d10 for Base Form, then add Unique Feature and Special Attack from the tables.</p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa021Husks","name":"Husks (Swarm)","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":5,"max":5},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":10},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":100,"instinct":20,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Half-Formed Caliban Clones</strong></p><p>Half-formed clones. Sanded down features. No exposed orifices or eyes. Everything a blank, featureless slate. They grow out of the walls, sliding off and slapping the ground when finished.</p><p><strong>Attack:</strong> Mindless Clawing - Wounds x d10 DMG</p><p><strong>Combat:</strong> Wounds x 10</p><p><strong>Swarm:</strong> This creature's Wounds represent the number of creatures in the Swarm. Combat and damage are based on current Wounds.</p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa022WireMn","name":"The Wire Man","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":200,"max":200},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":5},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":0,"instinct":0,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>10-Story Behemoth</strong></p><p>10 story tall faceless behemoth built entirely of wires. Stomps reverberate across The Sink. Easy to hide from but he peers into cracks and broken windows.</p><p><strong>Attack:</strong> Massive Swipe 1d100 DMG (Body Save to avoid)</p><p><strong>Behavior:</strong> Retreats after gaining a Wound.</p><p><em>The Wire Man is best used as an environmental hazard, not an enemy. It shapes the landscape.</em></p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa023Calban","name":"Caliban","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":200,"max":200},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":2},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":50,"instinct":85,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Formerly Dr. Bancali - The Infection Itself</strong></p><p>Fused into the wall of his Inner Chamber, pathetic and mutilated. His human form is unrecognizable and he cannot speak, only rasp out machine-assisted breaths.</p><p><strong>Reinforcements:</strong> Caliban himself cannot fight, though he can call Chokespawn, Husks, or attempt to compel Infected Level 6+ to do his bidding (Sanity Save to resist). Reinforcements arrive within 1d10 rounds.</p><p><strong>Hard to Kill:</strong> Caliban is more of a loose hive mind at this point rather than a person, and makes a great campaign-length villain.</p><ul><li>If the entire Dream is destroyed, there is a 10% chance Caliban escaped on some other Infected person or machine.</li><li>If his original form in the Inner Chamber is killed, Prospero's Dream starts to fall apart. It will self destruct in 1d10 hours.</li></ul>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa024Avatar","name":"Avatar of Caliban","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":50,"max":50},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":5},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":80,"instinct":65,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Caliban's Primary Physical Form</strong></p><p>Seven feet tall. Naked but covered in wires. Caliban's primary form when interacting physically with denizens of The Dream. His crown drags several meters of wire behind it like a train.</p><p><strong>Attack:</strong> Tendril x2 2d10 DMG + Infection</p><p><strong>Awful Crown:</strong> Can command any machine to do wearer's bidding. Characters with cybermods/slickware and androids get Sanity Saves to resist.</p><p><em>Warning: This can be an insta-kill. Telegraph this ability early by having Caliban command a minor weapon or inert object to explode.</em></p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa025Jealsy","name":"Jealousy of Caliban","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":45,"max":45},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":5},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":80,"instinct":20,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Caliban's Guardian Beast</strong></p><p>A grossly enlarged former human, swollen with fat, metal plates and tubes fused into its flesh. Barrels of projectile weapons extrude from chest, mouths, eyes, and arms. Hands terminate in brick-like metal boxes, skin wrapped around it like a disguise.</p><p><strong>Attacks:</strong> Bash 5d10 DMG or Fleshcannon 3d10 DMG</p><p><strong>Fleshcannon:</strong> Shoots disgorged limbs, viscera, and blood at target. Infection Check [-].</p><h3>Garbled Screams:</h3><ul><li>\"Stay away from her!\"</li><li>\"Only I can find the cure!\"</li><li>\"Why won't you leave us alone?\"</li></ul>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa026Guile","name":"Guile of Caliban","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":35,"max":35},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":3},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":40,"instinct":65,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":10,"max":10},"description":"<p><strong>Caliban's Hunter</strong></p><p>Fast crawling beast with six arms. Silent movement. Can crawl on walls and ceilings as fast as the floor. Ambushes and then retreats. Always runs away after gaining a Wound.</p><p><strong>Attacks:</strong> Slash x2 2d10 DMG or Tranq Lash 1d10 DMG or Bloodsucker Bite</p><p><strong>Armor:</strong> 10 (Camouflage)</p><p><strong>Tranq Lash:</strong> Body Save or knocked unconscious for 1d5 rounds.</p><p><strong>Bloodsucker Bite:</strong> 1d10 DMG, doubled if target is unconscious. Heals the Guile for 1 Wound.</p><p><em>See if you can make the Guile of Caliban a recurring villain, something that stalks the players.</em></p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
{"_id":"APOFa027Rage","name":"Rage of Caliban","type":"creature","img":"systems/mosh/images/icons/ui/default-actor.png","system":{"health":{"value":30,"max":30},"wounds":{"value":0,"max":4},"stress":{"value":0,"max":20,"min":0},"combat":80,"instinct":65,"hits":1,"armor":{"value":0,"max":0},"description":"<p><strong>Caliban's Berserker</strong></p><p>Grotesquely musclebound creature found in Cell 4A of The Court's Holding Cells. Its features are a puffy mess of flesh and bone.</p><p><strong>Attacks:</strong> Bash 3d10 DMG or Mutated Arm Cannons 1d100 DMG</p>"},"prpinitems":[],"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.0","coreVersion":"13","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null}}
